WEBVTT

1
00:00:12.734 --> 00:00:19.107
Dr. Dolittle and the animals missed Polynesia and Chee-Chee very much.

2
00:00:19.108 --> 00:00:23.921
But they knew Polynesia and Chee-Chee were happier in Africa.

3
00:00:23.922 --> 00:00:28.156
"Where are we now, Dr. Dolittle?" asked Dab-Dab.

4
00:00:28.157 --> 00:00:34.445
"I'm not sure," Dr. Dolittle scratched his head.

5
00:00:34.446 --> 00:00:38.230
"Dr. Dolittle! Dr. Dolittle!"

6
00:00:38.231 --> 00:00:41.037
Voices were calling from the sky.

7
00:00:41.038 --> 00:00:45.276
"Oh, hello!" the doctor waved to some birds.

8
00:00:45.277 --> 00:00:48.980
"You're going the wrong way!" one shouted.

9
00:00:48.981 --> 00:00:54.588
"These are Barbary waters!" another one said.

10
00:00:54.589 --> 00:00:59.164
"Barbary? What's that?" asked the doctor.

11
00:00:59.165 --> 00:01:02.580
"They're pirates," the other bird whispered.

12
00:01:02.581 --> 00:01:05.479
Dab-Dab began to shake with fear.

13
00:01:05.480 --> 00:01:12.096
"Pirates? Oh, no!" he quacked loudly.

14
00:01:12.097 --> 00:01:16.271
"The Barbary pirates wait for boats," explained the bird.

15
00:01:16.272 --> 00:01:19.794
"After they attack the boat, they steal everything in it."

16
00:01:19.795 --> 00:01:23.823
"The pirates take people, too," said another bird.

17
00:01:23.824 --> 00:01:28.527
"Sometimes, they throw people into the water!"

18
00:01:28.528 --> 00:01:32.265
Dr. Dolittle did not want to meet any pirates.

19
00:01:32.266 --> 00:01:33.615
"Go this way!

20
00:01:33.616 --> 00:01:36.741
You'll be safe!" the birds cried out.

21
00:01:36.742 --> 00:01:41.171
So the doctor sailed the boat away from the Barbary waters.

22
00:01:41.172 --> 00:01:44.090
"Whew! That was close!"

23
00:01:44.091 --> 00:01:47.908
Dr. Dolittle wiped his forehead.

24
00:01:47.909 --> 00:01:53.042
The next day, Dr. Dolittle forgot all about the Barbary pirates.

25
00:01:53.043 --> 00:01:59.473
"Mmmm . . . I smell roast beef . . . ," Jip was talking in his sleep.

26
00:01:59.474 --> 00:02:04.723
Dr. Dolittle laughed.

27
00:02:04.724 --> 00:02:10.669
"Apple pie . . . potatoes and . . . ," Jip mumbled.

28
00:02:10.670 --> 00:02:16.629
"Yummy! I smell roast beef!" Gub-Gub said happily.

29
00:02:16.630 --> 00:02:20.166
Dr. Dolittle sniffed the air.

30
00:02:20.167 --> 00:02:23.535
"Jip smells roast beef, too."

31
00:02:23.536 --> 00:02:27.062
"Maybe it's from that ship!" Gub-Gub pointed.

32
00:02:27.063 --> 00:02:31.909
"Uh, Doctor," Dab-Dab's voice shook.

33
00:02:31.910 --> 00:02:34.121
"Dogs have a good sense of smell.

34
00:02:34.122 --> 00:02:38.041
Almost as good as pigs," Gub-Gub said.

35
00:02:38.042 --> 00:02:45.388
"Dr. Dolittle . . . uh . . . ," Dab-Dab pointed but couldn't speak.

36
00:02:45.389 --> 00:02:49.780
"What is it, Dab-Dab?" Dr. Dolittle asked.

37
00:02:49.781 --> 00:02:53.755
Jip was still sleeping.

38
00:02:53.756 --> 00:02:56.325
"Trouble, bad men.

39
00:02:56.326 --> 00:03:05.139
I smell five, no, six men . . . grrrrrr," he growled.

40
00:03:05.140 --> 00:03:10.561
Then he barked so loudly he woke up.

41
00:03:10.562 --> 00:03:12.765
"I had a terrible dream.

42
00:03:12.766 --> 00:03:17.531
I . . . Dr. Dolittle!" Jip suddenly jumped up.

43
00:03:17.532 --> 00:03:21.792
A big ship with red sails was coming toward them.

44
00:03:21.793 --> 00:03:30.413
"It's the Barbary pirates," whispered Dab-Dab.

45
00:03:30.414 --> 00:03:32.668
Dr. Dolittle gave orders.

46
00:03:32.669 --> 00:03:36.736
"We must put more sails on our boat," he shouted.

47
00:03:36.737 --> 00:03:40.071
"Jip! Gub-Gub! Find all the sails.

48
00:03:40.072 --> 00:03:41.979
Bring them to me!"

49
00:03:41.980 --> 00:03:47.149
The pirate ship moved closer and closer.

50
00:03:47.150 --> 00:03:50.719
Dr. Dolittle used every sail on the boat.

51
00:03:50.720 --> 00:03:53.648
But the boat was still not fast enough.

52
00:03:53.649 --> 00:03:56.801
"What do we do?" cried Gub-Gub.

53
00:03:56.802 --> 00:04:03.215
"Too-Too! Find the birds!" Dr. Dolittle told the owl.

54
00:04:03.216 --> 00:04:06.139
Too-Too came back with two birds.

55
00:04:06.140 --> 00:04:09.530
"Only two birds?" barked Jip.

56
00:04:09.531 --> 00:04:13.078
"The rest are coming!" one bird called down.

57
00:04:13.079 --> 00:04:14.700
"Bring all the rope you have.

58
00:04:14.701 --> 00:04:19.470
Quickly!" shouted the other one.

59
00:04:19.471 --> 00:04:21.775
Dr. Dolittle brought the rope.

60
00:04:21.776 --> 00:04:26.148
"Make the rope into a lot of thin strings," said one bird.

61
00:04:26.149 --> 00:04:29.052
Soon they had hundreds of thin strings.

62
00:04:29.053 --> 00:04:32.182
Dr. Dolittle tied the ends to the boat.

63
00:04:32.183 --> 00:04:36.426
"Now what?" he asked the bird.

64
00:04:36.427 --> 00:04:39.562
Suddenly the sky started to get dark.

65
00:04:39.563 --> 00:04:42.172
There was a low rumbling sound.

66
00:04:42.173 --> 00:04:46.046
"What's that noise?" Gub-Gub asked.

67
00:04:46.047 --> 00:04:48.941
"I don't know," Jip replied.

68
00:04:48.942 --> 00:04:51.794
He did not push the pig away this time.

69
00:04:51.795 --> 00:04:55.518
"Look up there!" Too-Too shouted excitedly.

70
00:04:55.519 --> 00:05:01.295
Above them hundreds of birds covered the sky.

71
00:05:01.296 --> 00:05:04.038
Each bird took a piece of string.

72
00:05:04.039 --> 00:05:08.503
"Okay, everyone! Hang on!" said a little bird.

73
00:05:08.504 --> 00:05:11.127
Together, the birds pulled the strings.

74
00:05:11.128 --> 00:05:14.701
Dr. Dolittle's boat nearly flew in the air.

75
00:05:14.702 --> 00:05:19.650
It moved faster than the pirates' ship.

76
00:05:19.651 --> 00:05:23.825
All the animals, except Dab-Dab, began to laugh.

77
00:05:23.826 --> 00:05:28.259
"Yippee! This is fun!" shouted Jip.

78
00:05:28.260 --> 00:05:32.374
"Look! I'm flying!" cried Gub-Gub.

79
00:05:32.375 --> 00:05:38.226
Shortly, the red sails disappeared.
